            {"after": 3, "q": "What does Sancho tell Don Quixote the windmills really are?", "options": ["Watchtowers built by an enemy", "Windmills whose sails only look like arms", "Sleeping giants under a spell", "Statues left by ancient knights"], "correct": 1},
            {"after": 5, "q": "How does Don Quixote explain his defeat after crashing into the windmill?", "options": ["He admits he was simply wrong", "He blames Sancho for distracting him", "He claims an enchanter turned the giants into windmills to cheat him of glory", "He says Rocinante stumbled by accident"], "correct": 2},
            {"after": 6, "q": "According to the closing paragraph, what does this episode come to symbolize about Don Quixote?", "options": ["His skill as a real warrior", "His ability to see greatness in ordinary things and pursue his ideals despite constant proof he is wrong", "His growing distrust of Sancho", "His decision to abandon chivalry"], "correct": 1},
